  "label": "The text 'me' is mapped onto the cat hiding behind the chair",
  "description": "The bottom text 'me wondering what this dude's problem is' explicitly uses the pronoun 'me' to refer to the observer or creator of the meme. This 'me' is visually represented by the cat hiding behind the chair, which is a common meme trope symbolizing someone who is confused, annoyed, or dismissive of the yelling. The mapping is established by the juxtaposition of the text and the visual, where the cat serves as the visual embodiment of the speaker's perspective.",
